Fixed and verified. The bug was in `advanceTurn` at src/sim.ts:43 — the growth gate was `foodSurplus >= 0`, so a settlement whose production exactly equaled consumption (surplus of 0) still gained a population point every turn, compounding turn after turn. The doc comment says growth requires an actual surplus, so I changed it to `foodSurplus > 0`.

Verification:
- Project `tsc --noEmit` and `vitest run` both pass (4/4 tests).
- Ran the real `advanceTurn` against three scenarios: break-even (2 farms, pop 5, 10 produced / 10 consumed) → pop stays 5; surplus (3 farms) → pop 6, food +5 banked; deficit (1 farm) → pop stays 5, food floored at 0.

No other changes — the food accounting was already correct, only the growth comparison was wrong.


